-#define RING_BUF_SIZE 1024
+// The RX ISR drains the UART/USB-CDC FIFO into this ring; schedIn (rateGroup10Hz)
+// empties it into the buffer pool. A fast host burst (e.g. the file-uplink START
+// sequence) can deliver more bytes than one 100 ms tick drains, so the ring must
+// absorb the burst -- on overflow the ISR drops bytes, which silently corrupts
+// the raw byte-stream passthrough to LoRa (every downstream frame then fails the
+// flight-side HMAC auth). The GDS uplinker delivers occasional multi-KB bursts
+// mid-transfer (observed ~5 KB at once) despite the per-chunk cooldown, so the
+// ring must absorb a whole burst; 16384 covers the observed worst case with margin.
+#define RING_BUF_SIZE 16384
 
